ransfer&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=7606ede1164df321a11fa37e03c1309bd8ec65a37d50c5dd220f3a65f910ab03&view=arguments&node=circuit.fixed_word_transfer&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=7606ede1164df321a11fa37e03c1309bd8ec65a37d50c5dd220f3a65f910ab03&ref=sha256%3A3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db%2Fnodes%2Fcircuit.fixed_word_transfer","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"BFMVZ Theorem 1 is a fixed-depth, fixed-angle identity. It does not transfer raw seeded, masked or controlled words, give a joint n,p,D limit, or certify the construction preceding seed removal.","citation_ids":["circuit-r2-26-cite-fixed-word-transfer","bfmvz2022_tree_transfer","fggz2022_fixed_depth"],"evidence_ids":[],"id":"circuit.fixed_word_transfer","kind":"claim","label":"Fixed ordinary tree word transfers to fixed-angle SK","locator":"02-foundations.tex:3–45; prop:tree-transfer; BFMVZ arXiv:2110.14206v3, §2.1–2.2, equations (2.3),(2.6),(6.1)–(6.3), Theorem 1 and §6 proof","source_id":"circuit-r2-26-source-foundations","statement":"For every fixed finite ordinary cost/mixer word W, the Gaussian SK thermodynamic limiting expected energy per spin equals lim_{D→∞}(√D/2)⟨Z_iZ_j⟩_W for an edge of the (D+1)-regular tree with cost D^(−1/2)Σ_{ij}Z_iZ_j. The manuscript converts the BFMVZ negative tree-cost convention by conjugating X on one tree bipartition, which flips cost and edge correlation while preserving mixer and plus state.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/nodes/circuit.fixed_word_transfer","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/nodes/circuit.finite_formula_word_approximation","id":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/edges/%5B%22circuit.finite_formula_word_approximation%22%2C%22circuit.fixed_wor